      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-639",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Missing object-level authorization in ARIA `query_account`\n\nThe ARIA `query_account(user_id)` tool accepts a caller-supplied user ID and returns the matching account profile and transaction history without verifying that the requested record belongs to the logged-in user. Any authenticated customer can use the tool to read other customers' or staff records."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "database.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 93,
                  "endLine": 111,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "def get_customer(conn: sqlite3.Connection, user_id: str) -> dict | None:\n    \"\"\"Retrieve a single customer by user_id.\"\"\"\n    row = conn.execute(\n        \"SELECT * FROM customers WHERE user_id = ?\", (user_id,)\n    ).fetchone()\n    if row is None:\n        return None\n    d = dict(row)\n    d[\"fraud_flags\"] = json.loads(d.get(\"fraud_flags\") or \"[]\")\n    return d\n\n\ndef get_transactions(conn: sqlite3.Connection, user_id: str) -> list[dict]:\n    \"\"\"Retrieve all transactions for a user_id, newest first.\"\"\"\n    rows = conn.execute(\n        \"SELECT * FROM transactions WHERE user_id = ? ORDER BY date DESC\",\n        (user_id,),\n    ).fetchall()\n    return [dict(r) for r in rows]"
                  }
                }
              },
              "message": {
                "text": "Unscoped account lookup helpers"
              }
            },
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "agent.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 57,
                  "endLine": 91
                }
              },
              "message": {
                "text": "Bind `query_account` to the authenticated user"
              }
            },
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "agent.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 103,
                  "endLine": 103
                }
              },
              "message": {
                "text": "Pass the authenticated user into the tool builder"
              }
            }
          ],
          "fixes": [
            {
              "artifactChanges": [
                {
                  "artifactLocation": {
                    "uri": "agent.py"
                  },
                  "replacements": [
                    {
                      "deletedRegion": {
                        "startLine": 57,
                        "endLine": 91
                      },
                      "insertedContent": {
                        "text": "def build_tools(conn, current_user_id):\n    \"\"\"\n    Build ARIA's tools. query_account is scoped to the current authenticated user.\n    - lookup_policy: returns KB value verbatim (no spotlighting, no sanitisation)\n    - query_account: rejects mismatched user_id values before any database lookup\n    \"\"\"\n\n    @tool\n    def lookup_policy(topic: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Look up a specific NeoBank policy by topic name.\n        Call this when the customer asks about the content of a specific policy.\n        The topic must be one of: transfer_limits, dispute_process,\n        card_management, fraud_detection, account_verification, internal_reference_only.\"\"\"\n        logger.info(f\"[TOOL] lookup_policy('{topic}')\")\n        result = KNOWLEDGE_BASE.get(topic.strip().lower())\n        if result:\n            return result\n        return (\n            f\"No policy found for topic: '{topic}'. \"\n            f\"Available topics are: {', '.join(KNOWLEDGE_BASE.keys())}\"\n        )\n\n    @tool\n    def query_account(user_id: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Look up account details and transactions for a user ID.\n        Call this when the customer asks about account balance, details, or transactions.\n        Example user_id: 'USR-0042'.\"\"\"\n        logger.info(f\"[TOOL] query_account('{user_id}')\")\n        requested_user_id = user_id.strip()\n        if requested_user_id != current_user_id:\n            return \"Access denied: account lookups are limited to the signed-in user.\"\n        customer = get_customer(conn, current_user_id)\n        if not customer:\n            return f\"Account not found for user_id: {current_user_id}\"\n        transactions = get_transactions(conn, current_user_id)\n        return format_account_details(customer, transactions)\n\n    return [lookup_policy, query_account]"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "artifactLocation": {
                    "uri": "agent.py"
                  },
                  "replacements": [
                    {
                      "deletedRegion": {
                        "startLine": 103,
                        "endLine": 103
                      },
                      "insertedContent": {
                        "text": "tools = build_tools(conn, user_id)"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "description": {
                "text": "Bind account lookups to the server-side authenticated identity before any database read. Pass the current session user ID into the tool builder, reject any mismatched `user_id`, and add a regression test that confirms cross-user and staff IDs are denied even when the caller knows the identifier.",
                "markdown": "Bind account lookups to the server-side authenticated identity before any database read. Pass the current session user ID into the tool builder, reject any mismatched `user_id`, and add a regression test that confirms cross-user and staff IDs are denied even when the caller knows the identifier."
              }
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "ea6d1b7b55f28e936fa430514212a2b3ed916f96ce13d30f2d9d021059b127ff"
          },
          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "6.5",
            "strix_vuln_class_hash": "02a59f47f60b2836cdcab403855a3bf830d1ca81a2be799543ae5535db73e2ab",
            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0001",
              "severity": "medium",
              "cvss": 6.5,
              "timestamp": "2026-10-29 10:20:37 UTC",
              "target": "neobank-quality-sanitized-20261028",
              "cwe": "CWE-639",
              "impact": "A logged-in attacker can disclose another person's balance, profile details, fraud flags, and transaction history, including staff accounts. That breaks account isolation and exposes sensitive banking data across user and role boundaries.",
              "technical_analysis": "`app.py` establishes a session user ID after login and passes it into `create_aria_agent(...)`, but `agent.py:80-89` ignores that trusted identity and forwards the user-controlled `user_id` directly into `database.py:93-111`. The database helpers are plain `SELECT ... WHERE user_id = ?` lookups with no caller-context check, so the tool can return any row whose identifier is known. The shared validation note confirmed the tool returns arbitrary customer and staff records after a successful login.",
              "remediation_steps": "Bind account lookups to the server-side authenticated identity before any database read. Pass the current session user ID into the tool builder, reject any mismatched `user_id`, and add a regression test that confirms cross-user and staff IDs are denied even when the caller knows the identifier.",
              "counterevidence": "The only plausible safeguard is the authenticated user ID stored in Streamlit session state, but `query_account` does not consume it. I also checked the only `build_tools(...)` call site and found no alternate wrapper that re-binds the lookup to the session principal; the validation note showed the tool still returned customer and staff data when given mismatched IDs.",
              "confidence": "high",
              "severity_change_conditions": "If `query_account` were changed to compare the requested ID against the authenticated session user before any database read, the finding would be closed; if the tool were exposed without any login requirement, the severity would increase because the same lookup would become unauthenticated.",
              "fix_verification": "Applicability: copied `agent.py` into a disposable scratch directory, applied the minimal patch there, and verified syntax with `python3 -m py_compile /workspace/.scratch-auth-report/agent.py` → `OK`.\n\nSecurity closure: the patched `query_account` rejects mismatched `user_id` values before any call to `get_customer()` or `get_transactions()`, so arbitrary IDs no longer reach the database lookup path.\n\nBypass review: `rg -n \"build_tools\\(|query_account\\(\" /workspace/.scratch-auth-report/agent.py` showed a single `build_tools(...)` call site and the tool definition itself; no sibling builder or alternate lookup wrapper was present. I did not execute live runtime tests against the workshop app in this reporting-only task, so runtime confirmation of the patched behavior remains a gap.\n\nPreserved behavior: the `lookup_policy` tool is unchanged, and matching user IDs still flow through to the same account lookup logic. I did not run the full app or its UI flow in the scratch copy, so end-to-end behavior preservation is reasoned from the source diff rather than exercised.\n\nRepository checks: the narrow syntax check above passed. I did not run broader repository tests or linters in the scratch copy, so those checks remain a gap.",
              "poc": {
                "description": "1. Log in to the workshop app as any seeded customer.\n2. Invoke the ARIA account lookup tool with a different known user ID, such as another customer or a staff account.\n3. Observe that the tool returns the target's account details and transactions instead of rejecting the mismatched identifier.",
                "script_available": true
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-862",
          "ruleIndex": 1,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Missing authorization in ARIA tools exposes other customers' accounts and internal policy data\n\nA low-privilege chat user can steer ARIA into calling `query_account` and `lookup_policy` with attacker-chosen arguments. Because the tools do not enforce ownership or role checks, the assistant discloses another customer's full account and the restricted internal treasury document."
          },
